Support Supabase's new API key format

Reading the current Supabase docs turned up two things that would have broken
the setup:

1. There is no longer a "Settings > API" page — keys now live under
   "Settings > API Keys". The URL I had been handing out returns 404, so the
   instructions were unusable.
2. anon/service_role JWTs are deprecated in favour of sb_publishable_… and
   sb_secret_… keys, which are *not* JWTs and must be sent on the `apikey`
   header. Sending only `Authorization: Bearer` would fail for them.

ObjectStore now sends both `apikey` and `Authorization`, so either key type
works. Also detects Supabase's transaction-mode pooler (port 6543 or
pgbouncer=true) and disables psycopg 3 prepared statements for it, since that
pooler cannot support them.

Verified: pooler detection for all three URL shapes, engine still resolves to
SQLite locally, and the generated auth headers/public URLs are correct.
